question:
Show that $f(x) = \frac{1}{2}\sin x, 0 \le x \le \pi$ represents probability density function for a random variable $x$. Calculate:
(i) $P\left(x \le \frac{\pi}{4}\right)$;
(ii) $P\left(x \ge \frac{\pi}{4}\right)$;
(iii) find $c$ such that $P(x \le c) = \frac{1}{2}$.

For a Binomial distribution with 5 trials and $p = 0.25$, find the probability that:
(i) all five trials are successful;
(ii) only four trials are successful;
(iii) at least three trials are successful;
(iv) none of the trials is successful.
